# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Test coverage and profiling output
coverage.*
cover.html
*.cover
*.prof
*.pprof

# Go workspace / tooling
go.work
go.work.sum
/vendor/

# Local state accidentally produced by manual runs
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.log

# Local environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private key material. The *public* half of the release signing key is tracked
# on purpose — cosign.pub and internal/updater/cosign.pub, which the release
# workflow checks are byte-identical — and none of the rules below match it.
# Only the private half must never be committed: `cosign generate-key-pair`
# writes cosign.key straight into the working directory, one `git add -A` away
# from being public forever, and a leaked signing key means every release
# signature has to be rotated. A fixture that genuinely needs one of these
# extensions can still be added with `git add -f`.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
cosign.key
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# Node tooling installed locally for the markdown checks
node_modules/

# lychee-action drops this into the workspace during the link check. GoReleaser
# refuses to build from a dirty tree, and the link check runs before it in the
# release workflow, so an untracked directory here fails the release.
lychee/
.lycheecache

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
*.tmp
*.bak
.idea/
.vscode/

# Internal working documents: specifications, plans, audits and agent tooling.
# These drive the work but are not part of the published repository.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
/*_AUDIT.md
